# Festag — dark-mode CTAs

In **dark / OLED** auth and onboarding chrome, primary and ghost CTAs share one quiet slate fill until the form is ready.

## Geometry

Auth CTAs and fields use **`--festag-auth-radius: 12px`** — soft premium rects on 46–48px controls.

- CTAs / inputs: `12px`
- Icon buttons (36px): `--festag-auth-radius-sm` / `10px`
- Textareas: `--festag-auth-radius-lg` / `14px`
- **Not** marketing pills (`999px`) and **not** portal-dense `8px`

## Idle (empty / invalid / not ready)

Both primary and ghost stay **darker / quieter** on OLED `#000`:

```css
background: rgba(186, 194, 210, 0.08); /* --festag-btn-dark-bg */
color: rgba(228, 228, 234, 0.90);
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
border-radius: var(--festag-auth-radius, 12px);
```

Hover/active idle lifts only slightly.

## Ready (valid input → `--ready`)

Only the **primary** action flips to Festag Night soft cool-white after successful input (e.g. valid email):

```css
background: #F0F2F5; /* --festag-btn-ready-bg */
color: #1A1A1E;
border: 1px solid transparent;
```

Hover `#DCE1E8` / active `#CFD5DD`. Ghost / secondary stay at idle density.

## Tokens

Idle uses `--festag-btn-dark-*` from `components/auth/auth-chrome-tokens.ts`. Ready uses `--festag-btn-ready-*` (Festag Night soft white). Radius lives on `.al-root` + chrome vars.

## Do not

- Make idle primary and ready primary look the same
- Force `--ready` on empty invite / empty name fields / incomplete emails
- Give ghost the ready white fill (skip / secondary stays quiet)
- Reintroduce full-pill `border-radius:999px` on auth CTAs/inputs
- Drop auth radius back to portal `8px` without an explicit ask
- Reintroduce harsh pure `#ffffff` ready when Festag Night soft white is intended

See also `festag-light-mode-ctas.mdc` (light stays white fills) and `festag-auth-no-field-borders.mdc`.
